<title>UK: CCDQ launches $250 million four-year Eurobond.</title>
<headline>CCDQ launches $250 million four-year Eurobond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Caisse Centrale Desjardins du Quebec has launched a $250 million four-year Eurobond, Merrill Lynch and Paribas said on Wednesday as joint lead managers.</p>
<p>The deal was priced to yield 32 basis points over the three-year U.S. Treasury note.</p>
<p>+ + +</p>
<p> AMT	  $250 MLN  COUPON     6.75	MATURITY    17.APR.01</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.247   PAY DATE    17.APR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.625     REOFFER    99.872    SPREAD	+32 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AA3	 LISTING    LONDON    PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA	  DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/GB/CA</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    QUEBEC    HOME CTRY  CANADA    TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.25	SELL CONC  1.375     PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 5.875 PCT U.S. TREASURY NOTE DUE 15.FEB.00 -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
